Approach (Valid Parentheses)

We use a stack to check if the brackets are valid.

Traverse the string character by character.
If the character is an opening bracket (, {, [:
Push its corresponding closing bracket ), }, ] into the stack.
If the character is a closing bracket:
Check if the stack is empty → return false.
Otherwise, pop from stack and check if it matches the current closing bracket.
If not matching → return false.
After traversal, if the stack is empty → valid parentheses.
If stack is not empty → invalid.

Complexity
Time Complexity	O(n)
Space Complexity	O(n)
